{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0203","billNumberShort":"H.B. 203","billNumberLong":"HB0203S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0045","shortTitle":"Non-Compete Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"CLANCT","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Clancy, Tyler","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"BALDEH","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Balderree, Heidi","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions relating to non-compete agreements.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits an employer from enforcing a non-compete agreement against an employee under certain conditions;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits a person from enforcing a non-compete agreement against an independent contractor;<hr><ltbullet>requires that an employer presenting an employee with an offer of employment include with the offer of employment a non-compete agreement if the employer intends to enter into a non-compete agreement with the employee;<hr><ltbullet>imposes requirements on an employer presenting an employee with a non-compete agreement;<hr><ltbullet>requires that an employer give an employee advance notice of a non-compete agreement;<hr><ltbullet>makes void a non-compete agreement under certain conditions;<hr><ltbullet>provides that a person that fails to comply with provisions that this bill enacts may not enforce a non-compete agreement;<hr><ltbullet>grants a right of action to an individual against a person that attempts to enforce an unlawful non-compete agreement; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Austin Weenig","fiscalAnalyst":"Alejandra G Rodriguez","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"DOYVUQYOHK","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-0